[[0,2444643,0,1,0,1,"2018-03-14T00:31:52","Joe_McCarthy","",[],"","Could Trump and Sessions send federal troops to California over immigration?","https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/2018/03/13/trump-sessions-might-send-federal-troops-california-immigration-laws-glenn-reynolds-column/417633002/","OccidentalEnclave"],[1,12169612,0,0,0,0,"2018-03-14T00:39:24","derram","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://archive.fo/H8Ik9\">https://archive.fo/H8Ik9</a> : \n</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Could Trump and Sessions send federal troops to California over immigration? </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>'Sessions’ stern warning was prompted by California laws designed to frustrate the enforcement of federal immigration laws, as inspired by the “Sanctuary City” movement. ' </p>\n<p>'It wouldn’t be the first time a president has sent troops to enforce federal law when local officials stood in the way. ' </p>\n<p>'United States, which struck down a federal law that tried to force local law enforcement to perform background checks on gun purchases. ' </p>\n<p>'The federal government can’t force state officials to administer or execute a federal law. ' </p>\n<p>'Federal law is 'the supreme law of the land.' I would invite any doubters to Gettysburg, and to the graves of John C. Calhoun and Abraham Lincoln.&quot;'</p>\n<hr />\n<p><a href=\"https://vgy.me/IFbuLh.png\">This has been an automated message.</a></p>"],[1,12169717,0,0,0,0,"2018-03-14T00:52:54","Joe_McCarthy","",[],"<p>Expect active civil disobedience from Mexican US servicemen a/o armed rebellion in California if this happens. That'd be a positive development.</p>"],[1,12170634,0,0,0,0,"2018-03-14T02:46:11","Thisismyvoatusername","",[],"<p>Interesting. Just earlier today I was thinking there’s no real need to wait for California to secede. We can just go ahead and move straight to the Reconstruction phase.</p>"]]
